issue.body:
I wanted only warnings and above to reach stdout, so I wrapped the stdout writer in a `FilteredLevelWriter`:

```ts
import { NewLogger, FilteredLevelWriter, LevelWriterAdapter, StdoutWriter, Level } from "ctx-log";

const w = new FilteredLevelWriter(new LevelWriterAdapter(StdoutWriter), Level.WarnLevel);
const log = NewLogger(w);
log.Warn().Msg("disk almost full");
log.Error().Msg("disk full");
```

**Expected:** both lines are printed.
**Actual:** only the `warn` line is printed; the `error` line is silently dropped. Same for `fatal`.

Looking at `src/log/writer.ts`, `WriteLevel` does `if (level >= this.Level)` on the level *strings*, so `"error" >= "warn"` is false alphabetically.

- ctx-log 0.0.7
- Node v20.11.1, macOS 14
